<title>MOROCCO: Morocco farm credit bank staff to strike - union.</title>
<headline>Morocco farm credit bank staff to strike - union.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Staff at Morocco's state-owned farmers' credit bank Caisse Nationale de Credit Agricole (CNCA) will strike for two days from June 4, a union spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>CNCA staff have already held two one-day strikes early this year to press for a revision of the salaries scale and for recognition of union membership, a spokesman affiliated to the Democratic Labour Confederation (CDT) said.</p>
<p>&quot;This is our third strike this year...despite talks with the management we reached no solution,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>There are 3,400 employees in the bank's 250 branches.</p>
<p>Bank officials were not available for comment.</p>
</text>
